r (prd006-cat R5.1-R5.4)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Module path is github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils per go.mod; binary entry point is cmd/cat/main.go with package main; no external dependencies beyond the Go standard library\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Apply transformations in the fixed order from prd006-cat R4.9: squeeze blanks (-s) first, then non-printing display (-v/-T), then end-of-line marker (-E), then line-number prefix (-n/-b); this order is non-negotiable per the spec\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Read input line-by-line using bufio.Reader.ReadBytes('\\\\n') rather than bufio.Scanner, so that partial last lines (no trailing newline) are preserved without reconstruction; the newline byte (when present) is included in the returned slice and must be preserved in output\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Handle SIGPIPE by catching syscall.SIGPIPE via os/signal and calling os.Exit(0) so that piping cat output to head or other truncating consumers exits cleanly without a broken-pipe error message, matching gcat behavior (prd006-cat R5.4)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"'go build ./cmd/cat/' succeeds with no errors and produces a runnable binary\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Default mode: all 256 byte values (0x00-0xFF) pass through without corruption when no flags are active; output bytes are identical to input bytes\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"-n produces format '     N\\\\t' (6-wide right-justified number followed by tab) for every output line including blank lines; -b produces the same format for non-blank lines only, blank lines receive no number and no tab; -b takes precedence over -n when both are given\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"-s with input containing four consecutive blank lines produces exactly one blank line in output; squeezing applies across file boundaries so the last blank line of one file and the first blank line of the next file count as con